# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Gray-Scott sanitizer preset (host-cpu-asan, #13).
#
# Every entry is a library outside the miniapp that keeps memory until process
# exit by design. None of these stacks contains a miniapp frame: on 2026-11-07,
# 112 leak reports over 1, 2 and 4 ranks were checked and 0 had a frame from
# Miniapps/gray-scott. If a leak report ever shows one of our files, that is a
# real leak: fix it, do not add an entry here.
#
# Use: LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>:print_suppressions=0

# Open MPI keeps operator tables, component state and PMIx/libevent buffers
# alive until exit (ompi_op_base_op_select and friends).
leak:libmpi.so
leak:libopen-pal.so
leak:libopen-rte.so
leak:libpmix.so
leak:libevent
leak:libhwloc.so
leak:libfabric.so
leak:libucs.so
leak:libucp.so

# Pulled in by Open MPI's PMIx security plugins at MPI_Init.
leak:libcrypto.so

# Open MPI's components (mca_*.so), named because dlclose_noop.so keeps them
# mapped until exit; without it their frames read "<unknown module>".
leak:mca_

# VTK's logger (loguru) stores thread names in a static map for the process
# lifetime; the miniapp names its threads once at start-up.
leak:vtkloguru::set_thread_name
